✅ How Contentful Feature Flag Solution Works
Each HOC or component block in Contentful includes a field like component_version: 'mvp' | 'final'.

During next build, Next.js fetches this field via getStaticProps and uses it to render the correct version.

Editors can update the flag in Contentful to control what shows up — without any code changes.

Once deployed, teams can flip between versions instantly by editing content — no rebuild needed unless code changes.

✅ How ISR Works
ISR allows static pages built with getStaticProps to be re-generated in the background after deployment.

You define a revalidate interval (e.g. revalidate: 60) to trigger when the page should refresh.

On the next visit after that interval, the page is rebuilt in the background with fresh data (e.g. new flags).

It gives you the performance of static with the flexibility of dynamic updates — no full redeploy required.
